WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:23.224
Welcome to the latest Axiovo interface. Its name combines axiom, a foundational starting point for reasoning, and novo, meaning new. Discover research through the sidebar and the search bar, then explore the updated tutorial, archive navigation, reading tools and source-linked evidence.

00:00:23.424 --> 00:00:43.408
Axiovo brings four research archives together. Explore arXiv, bioRxiv, and ChemRxiv, plus the IACR Cryptology ePrint Archive for cryptography and quantum security. Choose the source that fits your subject.

00:00:43.608 --> 00:00:56.104
On arXiv Discover, open Archive subject and type part of a name or code. Typing quant brings up Quantum Physics and other matching categories.

00:00:56.304 --> 00:01:07.264
You can also type in the research subfield and subtopic dropdowns. Each dropdown offers choices within the path you have selected.

00:01:07.464 --> 00:01:19.480
Use the search field to enter the exact title, an author, or an arXiv identifier. Results link to their original paper record.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:34.072
Expand the advanced search settings. Specify a date or date range. Axiovo distinguishes verified complete date batches from partial source snapshots.

00:01:34.272 --> 00:01:43.312
For arXiv, the cross-list option can narrow results to records appearing in more than one subject category.

00:01:43.512 --> 00:01:52.768
Use author and affiliation fields to make a more precise query and read the source evidence before using a result.

00:01:52.968 --> 00:02:02.584
You can add personal topics and subtopics, save frequently used research paths, and restore defaults when needed.

00:02:02.784 --> 00:02:12.880
The bioRxiv Discover page has its own biology taxonomy, searchable topic selectors, and preprint search.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:22.672
ChemRxiv provides searchable chemistry subject and topic dropdowns while keeping the source of each paper visible.

00:02:22.872 --> 00:02:42.832
The Cryptology ePrint page opens records from the IACR archive, including quantum cryptography, post-quantum cryptography, signatures and security protocols. Type a research topic and select the matching suggestion to narrow indexed records.

00:02:43.032 --> 00:03:07.912
Search by title, author or a Cryptology ePrint identifier such as 2026 slash 1234. Read each source-linked abstract, save a paper to Library or compare its metadata. Because backfill is ongoing, always use the original IACR search when the local index lacks a paper.

00:03:08.112 --> 00:03:19.216
Open Research Desk to search all four preprint archives in one place. Results remain separated by their original archive.

00:03:19.416 --> 00:03:31.744
Enter research keywords in Research Desk, then click Search preprints to check arXiv, bioRxiv, ChemRxiv and Cryptology ePrint together.

00:03:31.944 --> 00:03:40.624
Expand Author, dates and sorting to narrow the cross-archive search before reviewing each source's coverage.

00:03:40.824 --> 00:03:48.280
Save a useful Research Desk search to repeat it later from the saved search list.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:04:00.208
Add papers to the comparison shortlist. Compare available metadata and abstracts side by side, then verify the originals.

00:04:00.408 --> 00:04:08.560
The Library gathers papers you saved from the different archives, with source and collection filters.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:18.376
Use the Library controls to create collections, filter saved papers, and organize your reading notes on this device.

00:04:18.576 --> 00:04:26.992
Select Following authors to review researchers you've saved, and inspect their available paper records.

00:04:27.192 --> 00:04:36.520
Library also contains project tools to organize research questions, keywords and associated references.

00:04:36.720 --> 00:04:47.128
Explore research recommendations based on your saved projects and interests. Always check the original source paper.

00:04:47.328 --> 00:04:56.152
Open Research Assistant and ask a focused question to retrieve source-linked evidence from indexed literature.

00:04:56.352 --> 00:05:09.256
Choose Inspect a paper and provide an arXiv ID or original link. The assistant distinguishes abstract claims from what still needs proof verification.

00:05:09.456 --> 00:05:21.376
Under Optional text and local model, choose evidence-only analysis, an on-device model, Ollama, or your own hosted API provider.

00:05:21.576 --> 00:05:38.728
For privacy, Axiovo does not ask for provider API keys in your browser. Hosted models require an administrator configured server. Until then, use source evidence or local models.

00:05:38.928 --> 00:05:49.216
Use the Sources panel to open original records, verify citations, and export a research session or evidence report.

00:05:49.416 --> 00:05:58.528
Open Research Tools to read local PDFs, use available annotations and explore research utilities.

00:05:58.728 --> 00:06:06.952
The paper workspace preserves version-exact arXiv links and supports personal research notes.

00:06:07.152 --> 00:06:17.032
Use Settings for preferences. Switch Night and Day appearance with the same accessible controls on every page.

00:06:17.232 --> 00:06:35.296
Recent announcements appear on the homepage and archive pages. Distinguish the first arXiv submission, version one, from later revisions. Source freshness and coverage notices tell you what has really been indexed.

00:06:35.496 --> 00:06:52.264
ProofLab is a separate research workspace for exploring technical questions, mathematical reasoning and research notes. Check the source evidence and calculations instead of assuming generated conclusions are verified.

00:06:52.464 --> 00:07:04.720
Choose Day or Night mode and one of five palettes in Settings. The new colors update navigation, panels and buttons across desktop and mobile.

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:19.816
The small Need help button can explain how to use Axiovo's features. Look for it on supported pages, and remember that external speech recognition may use the browser's own provider.

00:07:20.016 --> 00:07:35.848
On the homepage, Watch tutorial video and Interactive step-by-step guide now share exactly the same content space. Choose either option without having the tutorial jump above or below its controls.

00:07:36.048 --> 00:07:49.120
You've now seen Axiovo's main workflows. Search broadly, save carefully, and always open the original research record to verify technical claims.

